.TH MM 1 "August 2026" "mm 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mm \- decide what's next, never when
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mm
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIarguments\fR]
.br
.B man mm
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mm
is a personal CLI scheduler.
It answers
.I what to do right now
and never
.IR when .
There are no clocks and no calendar UI.
.PP
The daily ritual is:
.PP
.RS
.B mm onboard
.br
.B mm
.br
.B mm done
.RE
.PP
Bare
.B mm
is the same as
.BR "mm next" .
.SH MODEL
Three containers, in precedence order:
.TP
.B interrupt stack
LIFO. Real urgency only
.RB ( "mm add \-p" ).
Preempts everything, then unwinds like a call stack.
.TP
.B main queue
FIFO. Default work. While any
.B gate
item is open, non-gate work is unreachable.
.TP
.B quick queue
Sub-1-minute trivia
.RB ( "mm add \-q" ).
Never auto-surfaced mid-task. Flush with
.BR "mm flush-quick" .
.PP
A
.B gate
is dominant work.
With
.B strict_gate
on (the default),
.B mm onboard
refuses a new day while leftover gates still sit in the queue.
Park them honestly with
.B mm suspend
or
.BR "mm reset \-\-park-gates" .
.B mm reset
alone only clears the onboard lock. It does not freeze the queue.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Work
.TP
.B mm
.TQ
.B mm next
Show the active item and start its timer.
.TP
.B mm peek
Same glance, no timer.
.TP
.BI "mm done" " [id]"
Finish the active item (or that id) and advance.
.TP
.BI "mm add" " task"
Enqueue.
.B \-p
pushes an interrupt.
.B \-q
goes to the quick queue.
.TP
.BI "mm block" " [reason]"
Stuck: requeue and move on.
.TP
.BI "mm unblock " id " [\-\-front]"
Clear a block. Queue items can jump to the front.
.TP
.BI "mm suspend" " [id]"
Park without finishing.
.TP
.BI "mm resume" " [id]"
Bring one item back. Most recent if omitted.
.B \-\-all
restores every parked item.
.TP
.BI "mm move " id " queue|stack|quick [\-\-front]"
Reclassify, keep id and history.
.SS Day
.TP
.B mm onboard
Seed today's queue from config. Once per day.
.B \-n
overrides today's rotation count.
.B \-\-force
seeds even with leftover gates.
.B \-\-again
re-seeds today.
.TP
.B mm reset
Clear today's onboard lock. Queue stays put.
.B \-\-park-gates
suspends leftover gates.
.B \-\-drop-gates
removes them (not archived).
.TP
.B mm init
Write a starter
.IR ~/.mm/mm.toml .
.B \-\-force
overwrites.
.SS Habits
Repeating items. A book, a walk, a course \- same object.
Declared in
.I ~/.mm/mm.toml
as
.BR [[habits]] .
Due items are injected into
.BR queue ,
.BR stack ,
or
.B quick
when mm loads. Gap days on
.B repeat > 1
do not break the streak. A missed
.I due
day is marked missed.
.PP
When the day rolls over, today's due items sit at the front of the queue
(gates, then normals, by weight). Yesterday leftovers stay behind them
and are not marked missed while still open. Closing a leftover credits
that due date only.
.TP
.BI "mm habit add " name
.B \-t
type tag.
.B \-r
repeat days.
.B \-p
queue|stack|quick.
.B \-\-gate
.B \-w
weight.
.B \-\-order
1 = front of the queue;
.B "mm habit set " name " order none"
returns it to weight ordering.
.TP
.BI "mm habit set " name " field value"
Change
.BR position ,
.BR repeat ,
.BR enabled ,
.BR archived ,
.BR type ,
.BR gate ,
.BR weight ,
.BR description ,
.BR days .
.TP
.B mm habit list [\-t type] [query]
.TQ
.BI "mm habit find " query
Search name, type, tags, description.
.TP
.BI "mm habit log " "[name]"
Done / missed history and streak.
.TP
.BI "mm habit miss " name
Today did not happen. Streak resets. Open item dropped.
.TP
.BI "mm habit rm " name
.SS Obsidian
Bidirectional sync with today's daily note. Boolean properties match
.B obsidian
on each habit (or a slug of the name). Toggle in Obsidian or
.B mm done
— both sides update.
.B energy
is not a habit.
.TP
.B mm obsidian sync
Pull done-toggles, inject dues, push MM history. Also runs on
.B mm next
when
.B [obsidian]
is enabled in
.IR mm.toml .
Only a box that changed since the last sync counts as your edit;
.I ~/.mm/obsidian.json
holds the values both sides last agreed on, so closing an item in mm is
never mistaken for an uncheck.
.TP
.B mm obsidian watch
Poll today's note and sync within a second. Runs until Ctrl\-C.
.TP
.BR "mm obsidian autostart " on | off | status
Keep the watcher alive in the background across logins (macOS launchd).
macOS withholds Desktop and Documents from background agents, so grant the
interpreter it names Full Disk Access; the command refuses to report success
until it has seen the watcher running.
.SS Books
Books are a rotation source: courses, papers, anything you return to.
Omit the page count for a repeating daily checklist. Daily checklists are usually habits with
.B type = book
.
.TP
.BI "mm book add " title " [pages]"
Add one. Trailing integer is pages.
.B \-g
groups titles so they onboard together.
.TP
.BI "mm book progress " id " pages"
Log pages read. Required the same day to
.B mm done
a page-tracked book gate. Checklist books (pages 0) close with
.B mm done
and stay in rotation until
.BR "mm book done" .
.TP
.BI "mm book done " id
Drop it from rotation (finished the course).
.TP
.BI "mm book daily " N
How many book units onboard picks each day.
.TP
.B mm book list
.TQ
.BI "mm book rm " id
.TQ
.B mm book sync
Reconcile
.IR ~/.mm/books_config.json
into tracked state.
.B \-\-prune
drops titles no longer in that file.
.SS Inspect
.TP
.B mm status
.TQ
.B mm stats
.TQ
.B mm review
.TQ
.B mm session
.TQ
.B mm archive [today]
.TQ
.B mm log [n]
.TQ
.B mm export [json|md|csv]
.TP
.B mm rules show
Today's compiled plan, no writes.
.TP
.B mm rules validate
.TQ
.B mm rules strict on|off
Leftover-gate lock.
.TP
.B mm capacity [queue|stack|quick] [max]
.TQ
.B mm backlog [\-\-promote]
.TP
.B mm start [label]
.TQ
.B mm stop
.TP
.B mm undo
.TQ
.B mm find query
.TQ
.B mm help
This manual
.RB ( man\ mm ).
.SH CONFIGURATION
You edit two files. Everything else is mm's memory. Do not hand-edit it.
.PP
.I ~/.mm/mm.toml
is the schedule:
.BR [[habits]] ,
optional tracks, onboard, gates, capacity, rewards, and
.B [obsidian]
(vault path + daily folder).
If it is absent,
.I ~/.mm/mm.rules.json
is used (old format). If both exist, TOML wins.
.PP
Habits auto-queue when due. Tracks still need
.B mm onboard
and an
.B onboard.order
entry \- a track missing from
.B order
is silent.
.PP
Track types:
.TP
.B rotation
Cycling window over a list. Does not freeze on the first items.
Checklist books and plain
.B items
rotate by calendar day.
Named
.B books
(or
.B source = books )
reads the book tracker.
.TP
.B weekday
Mon–Sun table. Empty string is a rest day.
Use this for weekend-only study (business, economy) so those titles
do not leak onto a Tuesday.
.TP
.B static
.TQ
.B list
Same items every day.
.PP
.B dominant = true
makes the track a gate.
.B position
is
.BR gate ,
.BR front ,
or
.BR back .
.PP
Annotated example:
.I mm/data/mm.toml
in the source tree; it is also what
.B mm init
writes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.mm/mm.toml
Schedule, including
.BR [[habits]] .
You edit this.
.TP
.I ~/.mm/habits.json
Habit streaks, missed, last done. Owned by mm.
.TP
.I ~/.mm/books_config.json
Declared reading list (paged books). You edit this.
.TP
.I ~/.mm/state.json
Queue, stack, quick, backlog, archive, session. Owned by mm.
.TP
.I ~/.mm/books.json
Book progress. Owned by mm.
.TP
.I ~/.mm/mm.rules.json
Legacy schedule. Ignored when
.I mm.toml
exists.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MM_HOME
Data directory. Default
.IR ~/.mm .
.TP
.B MM_STATE
.TQ
.B MM_BOOKS
.TQ
.B MM_BOOKS_CONFIG
.TQ
.B MM_HABITS
.TQ
.B MM_RULES
Override individual files.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colour. Also disabled when stdout is not a terminal.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mm init
mm book add "PSY101"
mm book add "CS302"
mm book add "Thinking Mathematically"
mm book daily 2
mm rules validate
mm onboard
mm
mm done
.fi
.PP
Two books a day, cycling the whole list — not stuck at the top.
Weekend extras belong in a
.B weekday
track, not in the same book list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid config
.RB ( "mm rules validate" )
or argparse error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR python (1)
.PP
https://github.com/Toseef-Ahmad/mm
